  "question": {
    "text": "In a triangle $\\mathrm{ABC}$, let $\\angle \\mathrm{C}=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$. If $\\mathrm{r}$ is the inradius and $\\mathrm{R}$ is the circumradius of the the triangle $A B C$, then $2(r+R)$ equals"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$b+c$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$a+b$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$a+b+c$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$c + a$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n2 r+2 R=c+\\frac{2 a b}{(a+b+c)}=\\frac{(a+b)^2+c(a+b)}{(a+b+c)}=a+b \\quad\\left(\\text { since } c^2=a^2+b^2\\right)\n$$"
  }
}